; FILED: a RAGGED nested vector literal — NATIVE is the wrong side.
; The contract is a clean, catchable error naming the mismatched dimension.
; native -r : ()        (fabricates an empty shape, no raise, keeps running)
; vm        : "caught", and the condition's message is
;             "tensor-shape: nested vector is ragged - dimension 1 has length 1
;              but 2 was expected"
; The VM previously set a FATAL vm->error here, so `guard` could not intercept
; it and the whole program died; it now raises catchably. Gate this in
; corpus/41_tensor_literals.esk once native raises too.
(display (guard (e (#t "caught")) (tensor-shape #(#(1.0 2.0) #(3.0)))))
(newline)
(display (guard (e (#t "caught")) (tensor-ref #(#(1.0 2.0) #(3.0)) 0 0)))
(newline)
(display (guard (e (#t "caught")) (tensor-shape #(#(1.0 2.0) 3.0))))
(newline)
